course: dictionary
lesson: 617
title: Words from history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aztec starts with a capital letter, because it is a name. The Aztecs are a people, and Aztec is also a describing word for things from their culture. Reading the words around it tells you which one it is. «About 700 years ago a wandering people, the Aztecs or Mexica, settled in the Valley of Mexico.» Here the Aztecs are the people themselves.
explain: Look at «Aztec gods» and «the Aztec calendar». The word Aztec tells you which gods and which calendar, so it is describing a thing. It is an adjective, and it stays the same whether one thing or many things are being described.
explain: Some patterns are only inspired by Aztec art, and the name is sometimes thought to be inaccurate. So when you see Aztec on a pattern, ask: did this really come from the Aztecs, or is it just a name that was given to it? Check with a history book or a dictionary.
fact: The Aztecs were a people who built a great empire in what is now central Mexico.
fact: Their capital, Tenochtitlan, was built on a lake, and it ended when the Spanish conquered the empire.
fact: Aztec is a noun when it names the people, and an adjective when it describes things like Aztec gods or Aztec pyramids.
fact: «Aztec» starts with a capital letter, as it is a name.
fact: Some patterns called Aztec are inspired by their art, but the name is sometimes thought to be inaccurate.
exercise: «The Aztecs built their great city, Tenochtitlan, on a lake.» Where was Tenochtitlan built? | In a desert | Under the sea | On a mountain top | *On a lake
exercise: In the phrase «the Aztec calendar», what kind of word is Aztec? | A verb, because it shows an action | *An adjective, because it describes the calendar | A noun, because it names a people | An adverb, because it tells how
exercise: «About 700 years ago a wandering people, the Aztecs or Mexica, settled in the Valley of Mexico.» Find and copy one word that names a people. | Valley | settled | ago | *Aztecs
test: «The Aztecs used cocoa beans as money.» What were cocoa beans used for by the Aztecs? | As toys | As roof tiles | As fuel for fires | *As money
test: The Aztec Empire lasted until what ended it? | The end of the school year | The first train in Mexico | The invention of chocolate | *The Spanish conquest
exam: Which phrase uses Aztec as an adjective, describing something? | Valley of Mexico | *Aztec pyramids | The Aztecs settled | Mexica people
